description: Conventional Commits without AI Co-authored-by trailers
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git commits

- Use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): description` in English, imperative, no trailing period
- No commit body unless the user explicitly asks for one
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by` trailers, including:
  - `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
  - `Co-authored-by: Claude <...>` (any Claude / Anthropic variant)
- If the IDE injects a Co-authored-by line, strip it before finishing the commit/push
- After committing, verify with `git log -1 --format=%B` that no Co-authored-by remains
